ry><doc-number>0751630</doc-number><kind>A2</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-10065647-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>10065647</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-6009090-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>6009090</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1091516A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>T. GARAKU ET AL.: 'CDMA taju shingo no shinpuku seigen houshiki no teian' PROCEEDINGS 1 OF COMMUNICATION SOCIETY MEETING IN 1997, THE INSTITUTE OF ELECTRONICS, INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATION ENGINEERS 13 August 1997, (TOKYO), page 294, XP002946624</text><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The amplitude of a transmitted signal after multiplexed is calculated by an envelope calculating section (113). If the calculated amplitude value exceeds a permissible amplitude, a correction coefficient which is the difference between the amplitude value before correction and that after correction is calculated by a correction coefficient calculation section (114). A correction value is calculated by multiplying sections (115 and 116) by multiplying the correction coefficient by a filter coefficient. The correction value is susbtracted from the transmitted signal after filter operation by substractors (119 and 120). Thereby, the transmitted amplitude at a peak time is suppressed without increasing the number of filter operating circuits.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans cette invention, l'amplitude d'un signal émis après multiplexage est calculée par un dispositif de calcul à enveloppe (113). Si la valeur d'amplitude calculée dépasse une amplitude autorisée, un coefficient de correction représentant la différence entre la valeur d'amplitude avant correction et celle après correction est calculé par un dispositif de calcul de coefficient de correction (114). Une valeur de correction est calculée par des dispositifs de multiplication (115, 116), en multipliant le coefficient de correction par un coefficient filtre. La valeur de correction est déduite du signal transmis après l'opération de filtrage par des soustracteurs (119, 120). Ainsi, on supprime l'amplitude transmise à un moment de pointe sans augmenter le nombre de circuits de fonctionnement filtres.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all 